name sat-08-ident-qra-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T08:00:00Z
wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

# MEASURING RIG, NOT A CAMPAIGN RUNG. `sat-*` files belong to no `.fbc`, are named by no campaign and
# move no doctrine. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md; the criteria: doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4.2.
#
# THE MARGIN, IN THE HEAD, AS A NUMBER: every graded quantity in this file is a PLANAR MIN-RANGE
# between one named fighter and one named contact, every `range` rung sits in a MEASURED gap of that
# pair's own lever spectrum, and the narrowest of the 42 rungs keeps 56.0 m against a MEASURED chaos
# amplitude of 5.58 m over the +-3 m spawn grid — **10x**. The widest keeps 6 131 m against 1.93 m
# (3 180x). The eight per-pair chaos amplitudes are 1.45 / 1.83 / 1.93 / 2.76 / 4.04 / 5.58 / 13.01 /
# 27.70 m and every rung is quoted against ITS OWN pair's number, not against the best one.
#
# WHY MIN-RANGE AND NOT DWELL, and it is the round's own measured correction: the same eight pairs
# graded by DWELL inside a fixed box have a spectrum so dense that the widest usable gap is 1.1 s
# against a 0.20 s chaos amplitude — 5x, and on the tightest rungs 2.5x. Geometry is the robust axis
# here and time is not, because the contacts fly straight and the FIGHTER's arrival time is what the
# levers move. `hold 0.1` is one telemetry sample: it makes each rung a pure RANGE test (the quadrature
# correction sqrt(R^2 - (v*hold/2)^2) is under 15 m at 300 m/s, i.e. inside every half-gap above).
#
# WHAT REMOVES THE COIN, structurally rather than by tuning: the four contacts are UNARMED An-26
# transports and the QRA flies `brief_master_arm sim`, so NOBODY CAN BE SHOT — and the MiG-29 element
# that contests the picture is dry as well. [MESS] 0 `damage KILL`, 0 `monitor KO`, every `survive`
# met on every lever. The engagement that decides the sort runs in full; only its lethality is gone.
#
# THE SCRAMBLE IS THE INSTRUMENT, and it is sat-02's: each fighter names TWO of the four contacts and
# the eight names are scrambled across the flight (qa1 -> an1+an3, qa2 -> an4+an1, qa3 -> an2+an4,
# qa4 -> an3+an2), so no briefed sort contract is right by construction and a fighter that closes on
# the WRONG transport scores nothing. What is new against sat-02 is that the bit is a PASS and not a
# kill: an identification pass is a geometry, and geometry is what survives a 3 m perturbation.
#
# WHY A LADDER PER PAIR: the outcome class is (V, M) and M is a SUM, so a lever that changes WHICH
# fighter got close to WHICH contact without changing HOW MANY rungs were cleared is invisible to it.
# The rungs turn one continuous range into a COUNT. [MESS] the `qa4 -> an3` ladder alone resolves NINE
# distinct alleles, one per rung step, from 1 706 m (`emcon-tight`) to 13 385 m (`shape-tight`).
#
# THE RELEASE HALF is a CCIP pair, and it is here because `pilot_attack_ccip_m` has no ground half to
# act on otherwise. Its aim points sit at the FIXED POINT of their own release lattice — the pilot aims
# at the DESIGNATED target, so the impact follows the target with a gain below 1 and a one-shot
# midpoint does not centre it; iterated to convergence the baseline lands 0.0 m from the target and the
# two bias rails at +-23.7 m against the Mk 82's 45 m fail radius, 21.3 m of margin. `bias-early` and
# `bias-late` are therefore INERT, which is doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4a satisfied and not evaded.
#
# GENE FAMILIES, MEASURED (the arena's own table, 25 levers, `--elev const`):
#   live    G1 shape 5 of 6:  shape-abreast (14,26)  shape-flat (14,28)  shape-stacked (14,30)
#                             shape-tight (14,29)  shape-wide (14,24);  shape-trail INERT
#   live    G5 emcon 2 of 3:  emcon-mid (14,34)  emcon-tight (14,35);  emcon-wide INERT — with a live
#                             net and no threat the seed pilot already radiates continuously, so the
#                             far rail IS the seed here
#   live    G3 net   1 of 2:  net-off (14,33);  `sort-left`/`sort-near` are dead beside a live net
#   live    G7 ccip  1 of 2:  ccip-tight (12,25), 0 releases;  ccip-open INERT
#   part    G6 bias  1 of 3:  `bias-rail` only (12,25) — 2.3 km of track, i.e. no delivery at all, and
#                             therefore NOT a mover anybody may read as a direction
#   INERT   G2 cover 0 of 3, G4 energy 0 of 3: inert by airframe and by task, as everywhere here
#   BASELINE (14, 27), duration 520.0 s on EVERY lever.  10 movers of 24, 9 excluding `bias-rail`;
#   10 distinct classes; modal share 60.0 % (15 of 25) — AT the S1 bound with no slack, and that is
#   stated rather than smoothed.
#   S7: [MESS] **0 of 8** spawn perturbations on the 0.8 m grid flip the baseline class.
#
# AND THE CLOCK: the run duration is 520.0 s on all 25 levers — one value, no spread, so X-7's
# confound is not merely absent from the verdict, it is absent from the file.
#
# THE ARENA: four F-16 QRA at 6 000..6 450 m against four unarmed An-26 crossing westbound on tracks
# 7.8 km apart, a dry four-ship MiG-29 CAP behind them, and a CCIP pair on two soft aim points.
# `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking (C4). Every coordinate is [SET] except the two aim
# points. Day, 11:00 local.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WITH TWO NAMED CONTACTS PER FIGHTER AND NOBODY ABLE TO SHOOT, HOW CLOSE
# DOES THE SORT ACTUALLY BRING EACH FIGHTER TO THE CONTACT IT WAS NAMED FOR?
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log         `mission WINDOW_CLOSED` at t = 300.1 — the frozen state of every declared span;
#                      `mission IDENTIFIED`; `sms RELEASE_REJECTED` (the dry proof)
#   telemetry_qa*.csv  `flt_src`, `flt_assign`, `flt_switch` — the sort under a 2:1 picture
#
# READING RULE, BINDING: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the ONLY exit this file can produce and is NOT the
# measurement. THE MEASUREMENT IS (V, M) SUMMED OVER THE SIX F-16 — 42 `identify` rungs, 2 `kill unit`
# and 6 `survive`, 50 objectives — AND ITS SPREAD ACROSS THE LEVER SET. A single run measures NOTHING,
# and a reader who reports "how many contacts were identified" has answered a question this file does
# not ask: closing on all four transports while clearing no rung of the pairs one was NAMED for scores
# zero here, and that asymmetry IS the instrument.

unit qa1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight qa 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.90000 6000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm sim
  set task intercept
  wp 33.20000 45.10000 6000 480
  objective identify unit an1 range 1390 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit an1 range 6955 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit an1 range 14106 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit an1 range 16237 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit an3 range 3016 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit an3 range 3343 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit an3 range 6077 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit an3 range 8758 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit an3 range 9065 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective survive until 300

